{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function hydrate(\n   client: QueryClient, \n   dehydratedState: Partial<DehydratedState>, \n   options?: HydrateOptions): void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/hydration.ts#L306","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/hydration.ts:306"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Restores a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DehydratedState"},{"type":"text","value":" (as produced by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dehydrate"},{"type":"text","value":") into a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":"'s cache, typically to seed the\nclient with data already fetched on the server. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mutations"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queries"},{"type":"text","value":" are each optional on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dehydratedState"},{"type":"text","value":".\nQueries not yet in the cache are built from the dehydrated snapshot; queries that already exist are only updated\nwhen the dehydrated data is newer than what's already cached. Newly built queries have their "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchStatus"},{"type":"text","value":" reset\nto "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'idle'"},{"type":"text","value":" so they don't hydrate stuck in a fetching state. If a dehydrated query still had an in-flight\npromise, it is resumed via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"query.fetch()"},{"type":"text","value":" (reusing that promise as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialPromise"},{"type":"text","value":") rather than re-invoking\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"client"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The client whose cache is restored into."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"dehydratedstate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"dehydratedState"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Partial"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/DehydratedState.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DehydratedState"}]},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The dehydrated state, e.g. produced by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dehydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server."}]},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"dehydratedState-properties\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"dehydratedstate-properties","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dehydratedState"},{"type":"text","value":" properties"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built from "},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/DehydratedState.md#properties","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DehydratedState"}]},{"type":"text","value":". See the type above for what it changes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/HydrateOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HydrateOptions"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" merged into every restored query and mutation (on top of the\nclient's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultOptions.hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":"), and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deserializeData"},{"type":"text","value":" to reverse "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"serializeData"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"options-properties\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"options-properties","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" properties"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<a id=\"options-property-defaultoptions\">"},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"</a>"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultOptions?"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"object"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options applied to the queries and mutations restored from the dehydrated state."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultOptions.deserializeData?"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransformerFn"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transforms a query's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" after it is read from the dehydrated state, reversing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"serializeData"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultOptions.mutations?"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MutationOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Error"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default options merged into every mutation restored from the dehydrated state."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultOptions.queries?"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Error"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":", readonly "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":"[], "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"never"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default options merged into every query restored from the dehydrated state."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// dehydratedState was produced by `dehydrate` on the server\n// and sent to the client, e.g. embedded in server-rendered markup.\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nhydrate(queryClient, dehydratedState)","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"client","text":"client","level":3},{"id":"dehydratedstate","text":"dehydratedState","level":3},{"id":"dehydratedstate-properties","text":"dehydratedState properties","level":4},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":3},{"id":"options-properties","text":"options properties","level":4},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction hydrate(\n   client: QueryClient, \n   dehydratedState: Partial<DehydratedState>, \n   options?: HydrateOptions): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/hydration.ts:306](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/hydration.ts#L306)\n\nRestores a `DehydratedState` (as produced by `dehydrate`) into a `QueryClient`'s cache, typically to seed the\nclient with data already fetched on the server. `mutations` and `queries` are each optional on `dehydratedState`.\nQueries not yet in the cache are built from the dehydrated snapshot; queries that already exist are only updated\nwhen the dehydrated data is newer than what's already cached. Newly built queries have their `fetchStatus` reset\nto `'idle'` so they don't hydrate stuck in a fetching state. If a dehydrated query still had an in-flight\npromise, it is resumed via `query.fetch()` (reusing that promise as `initialPromise`) rather than re-invoking\n`queryFn`.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### client\n\n`QueryClient`\n\nThe client whose cache is restored into.\n\n### dehydratedState\n\n`Partial`\\<[`DehydratedState`](../interfaces/DehydratedState.md)\\>\n\nThe dehydrated state, e.g. produced by `dehydrate` on the server.\n\n<a id=\"dehydratedState-properties\"></a>\n\n#### `dehydratedState` properties\n\nBuilt from [`DehydratedState`](../interfaces/DehydratedState.md#properties). See the type above for what it changes.\n\n### options?\n\n[`HydrateOptions`](../interfaces/HydrateOptions.md)\n\n`defaultOptions` merged into every restored query and mutation (on top of the\nclient's `defaultOptions.hydrate`), and `deserializeData` to reverse `serializeData`.\n\n<a id=\"options-properties\"></a>\n\n#### `options` properties\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n| ------ | ------ | ------ |\n| <a id=\"options-property-defaultoptions\"></a> `defaultOptions?` | `object` | Options applied to the queries and mutations restored from the dehydrated state. |\n| `defaultOptions.deserializeData?` | `TransformerFn` | Transforms a query's `data` after it is read from the dehydrated state, reversing `serializeData`. |\n| `defaultOptions.mutations?` | `MutationOptions`\\<`unknown`, `Error`, `unknown`, `unknown`\\> | Default options merged into every mutation restored from the dehydrated state. |\n| `defaultOptions.queries?` | `QueryOptions`\\<`unknown`, `Error`, `unknown`, readonly `unknown`[], `never`\\> | Default options merged into every query restored from the dehydrated state. |\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n// dehydratedState was produced by `dehydrate` on the server\n// and sent to the client, e.g. embedded in server-rendered markup.\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nhydrate(queryClient, dehydratedState)\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: hydrate\ntitle: hydrate\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction hydrate(\n   client: QueryClient, \n   dehydratedState: Partial<DehydratedState>, \n   options?: HydrateOptions): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/hydration.ts:306](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/hydration.ts#L306)\n\nRestores a `DehydratedState` (as produced by `dehydrate`) into a `QueryClient`'s cache, typically to seed the\nclient with data already fetched on the server. `mutations` and `queries` are each optional on `dehydratedState`.\nQueries not yet in the cache are built from the dehydrated snapshot; queries that already exist are only updated\nwhen the dehydrated data is newer than what's already cached. Newly built queries have their `fetchStatus` reset\nto `'idle'` so they don't hydrate stuck in a fetching state. If a dehydrated query still had an in-flight\npromise, it is resumed via `query.fetch()` (reusing that promise as `initialPromise`) rather than re-invoking\n`queryFn`.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### client\n\n`QueryClient`\n\nThe client whose cache is restored into.\n\n### dehydratedState\n\n`Partial`\\<[`DehydratedState`](../interfaces/DehydratedState.md)\\>\n\nThe dehydrated state, e.g. produced by `dehydrate` on the server.\n\n<a id=\"dehydratedState-properties\"></a>\n\n#### `dehydratedState` properties\n\nBuilt from [`DehydratedState`](../interfaces/DehydratedState.md#properties). See the type above for what it changes.\n\n### options?\n\n[`HydrateOptions`](../interfaces/HydrateOptions.md)\n\n`defaultOptions` merged into every restored query and mutation (on top of the\nclient's `defaultOptions.hydrate`), and `deserializeData` to reverse `serializeData`.\n\n<a id=\"options-properties\"></a>\n\n#### `options` properties\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n| ------ | ------ | ------ |\n| <a id=\"options-property-defaultoptions\"></a> `defaultOptions?` | `object` | Options applied to the queries and mutations restored from the dehydrated state. |\n| `defaultOptions.deserializeData?` | `TransformerFn` | Transforms a query's `data` after it is read from the dehydrated state, reversing `serializeData`. |\n| `defaultOptions.mutations?` | `MutationOptions`\\<`unknown`, `Error`, `unknown`, `unknown`\\> | Default options merged into every mutation restored from the dehydrated state. |\n| `defaultOptions.queries?` | `QueryOptions`\\<`unknown`, `Error`, `unknown`, readonly `unknown`[], `never`\\> | Default options merged into every query restored from the dehydrated state. |\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n// dehydratedState was produced by `dehydrate` on the server\n// and sent to the client, e.g. embedded in server-rendered markup.\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nhydrate(queryClient, dehydratedState)\n```\n"}
